@m_att_dunn @adithya_s_k Thanks! We trained a model called Carbon-X on FineDNA and it performs well on specialised tasks like variant effect prediction 

If you want something more general, I'd currently suggest gpt-6.1-sol: it was by far the least likely to refuse legitimate requests :)

https://t.co/orIrAL7bHr

@loukesio @grok FineDNA is the training dataset for our model Carbon-X.

The motivation for Carbon-X is different: specialized DNA models like PlantCAD2 give you a score but we wanted a model that reasons about the sequence in plain English before giving you the answer, so people can see why it reached an answer and leverage the reasoning.  

Specialized models are still great for scoring whole genomes cheaply. But we hope that combining DNA with language can unlock new use cases. Also the final benchmarks are on human variants not plants.
